      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Wes Skiles Peacock Springs State Park is located in Suwannee County, northern

    Florida,
    within the Branford Karst Plain of the Ocala Karst District, on a marine

    terrace.
    The area is characterized by relatively flat karst terrain, with limestone at
    or

    near the surface, numerous sinkholes, springs, and an extensive network
    of

    submerged cave passages. The cave system developed primarily within the
    Ocala

    Limestone and forms part of the Floridan aquifer system.'
