    - target: {fileID: 8380166838820477280, guid: 923bf044c9adf4f638c3ec45852ca83d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Wes Skiles Peacock Springs State Park is located in Suwannee County,
        northern

        Florida, within the Branford Karst Plain of the Ocala Karst
        District, on a marine

        terrace. The area is characterized by relatively
        flat karst terrain, with limestone at or

        near the surface, numerous
        sinkholes, springs, and an extensive network of

        submerged cave passages.
        The cave system developed primarily within the Ocala

        Limestone and
        forms part of the Floridan aquifer system.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
